[rank0]:{"result": "# Decision Log\n\nKey decisions and their rationale, extracted from team discussions and blocker threads.\n\n---\n\n## DEC-001: Firm v1 SDK Deprecation Deadline\n\n- **Date:** 2026-03-15\n- **Context:** Dave Wilson raised concerns about the June 30 migration deadline for the API v2 Migration experiment (EXP-001), specifically the regression testing window.\n- **Decision:** The deadline is firm. v1 SDK reaches EOL on July 1, 2026.\n- **Action:** Prioritize regression testing in Sprint 25. No extensions.\n- **Participants:** Dave Wilson (raised concern), Alice Chen (decision maker)\n- **Source:** Thread 2 in discussion_threads.md\n\n---\n\n## DEC-002: Minimal Onboarding for Mobile Beta\n\n- **Date:** 2026-04-16\n- **Context:** Tight timeline for hitting the 1000-user beta target (OKR-002). Full onboarding flow would delay launch.\n- **Decision:** Ship with minimal onboarding. Iterate based on user feedback post-launch.\n- **Action:** Scope down onboarding tutorial screens (RUN-006) to essentials only.\n- **Participants:** Alice Chen, Bob Martinez\n- **Source:** Thread 5 in discussion_threads.md\n\n---\n\n## DEC-003: External Help for Security Documentation\n\n- **Date:** 2026-03-05\n- **Context:** SOC 2 audit scheduled for May. Three open gaps in access control documentation are blocker-critical for the Security Audit (EXP-004) and OKR-003.\n- **Decision:** Request external help for documentation gaps.\n- **Action:** Engage external compliance consultants to close documentation gaps before audit.\n- **Participants:** Alice Chen (requested), Dave Wilson (identified need)\n- **Source:** Thread 6 in discussion_threads.md\n\n---\n\n## DEC-004: Deprioritize Dark Mode Flicker\n\n- **Date:** 2026-04-20\n- **Context:** Dark mode toggle flickers (INC-005) was reported as S4-Trivial, not consistently reproducible.\n- **Decision:** Won't fix. Issue does not impact user workflows and occurs only in development environment.\n- **Action:** Close incident. No further investigation.\n- **Participants:** Eve Thompson (reporter), Dave Wilson (last editor)\n- **Source:** incident_log.csv INC-005\n"}
[rank0]:</tool_output><|eot|><|start|>tool read<|message|><tool_output name="read">
[rank0]:{"result": "# Discussion Threads\n\nTranscript of key comment threads from experiment pages, organized by topic.\n\n---\n\n## Thread 1: Auth Middleware Progress (EXP-001)\n\n- **Bob Martinez** (2026-05-01): The auth middleware migration is partially complete. We're handling the JWT verification changes now.\n- **Alice Chen** (2026-05-02): Good progress. Let's make sure we update the runbook docs once the new middleware is live.\n\n---\n\n## Thread 2: Migration Deadline Concerns (EXP-001 — Deadline Callout Block)\n\n- **Dave Wilson** (2026-03-15): Is there any flexibility on the June 30 deadline? Slightly concerned about the regression testing window.\n- **Alice Chen** (2026-03-15): The deadline is firm — the v1 SDK reaches EOL on July 1. We need to prioritize regression testing in Sprint 25.\n\n---\n\n## Thread 3: Mobile CI Flakiness (EXP-005)\n\n- **Eve Thompson** (2026-04-20): The iOS build is now consistently passing CI. Android still has a flaky test in the payment module.\n- **Bob Martinez** (2026-04-21): I'll look into flaky Android payment tests this sprint. Might be a race condition in the mock server setup.\n\n---\n\n## Thread 4: Safari 17 Crash (INC-001)\n\n- **Carol Davis** (2026-05-10): Safari 17 users are seeing a blank page after login. Looks like a JS compatibility issue with the auth redirect.\n- **Bob Martinez** (2026-05-11): Confirmed — it's the `globalThis` polyfill missing. Hotfix is ready, deploying to production tonight.\n\n---\n\n## Thread 5: Mobile Beta Scope (EXP-005 / OKR-002)\n\n- **Alice Chen** (2026-04-15): The beta launch timeline is tight. We may need to scope down the onboarding flow to hit the 1000-user target.\n- **Bob Martinez** (2026-04-16): Agreed. Let's ship with a minimal onboarding and iterate based on user feedback post-launch.\n\n---\n\n## Thread 6: Security Documentation Gaps (EXP-004 / OKR-003)\n\n- **Dave Wilson** (2026-03-01): SOC 2 audit is scheduled for May. We still have 3 open gaps in the access control documentation.\n- **Alice Chen** (2026-03-05): Can we get external help for the documentation gaps? This is blocker-critical.\n"}
