tatus | Priority |\n|-----|-------|----------|-------------|--------|----------|\n| RUN-001 | Migrate auth middleware to v2 SDK | 2026-05-20 | 64 days | In Progress | High |\n| RUN-002 | Update database connection pooling | 2026-05-15 | 69 days | In Review | Medium |\n\nBoth runs remain unfinished — the core auth migration task (RUN-001) has been stuck in-progress for over two months.\n\n#### Discussion Threads & Unresolved Blockers\n\n| Thread | Key Issue | Status |\n|--------|-----------|--------|\n| Thread 2 (Migration Deadline Callout) | Dave Wilson raised regression testing window concern; Alice Chen confirmed June 30 deadline firm | **Decision rendered** (DEC-001) but deadline missed |\n| Thread 4 (Safari 17 Crash) | Safari 17 blank-page bug traced to missing `globalThis` polyfill; hotfix deployed | Hotfix deployed — resolution pending verification |\n\n#### OKR Cross-Reference\n\n| OKR | Objective | Status | Impact |\n|-----|-----------|--------|--------|\n| OKR-001 | Scale platform to 10x users | On Track | At risk from downstream effects — p99 latency target (<200ms) depends on API v2 performance gains. A lagging migration threatens KR1. |\n\n#### Prior Decisions & Follow-Through\n\n| Decision | Action Assigned | Acted On? | Assessment |\n|----------|----------------|-----------|------------|\n| **DEC-001** (2026-03-15) | Prioritize regression testing in Sprint 25; no extensions to July 1 EOL deadline | ❌ **Not successfully acted upon** | Experiment reached 60% at its June 30 deadline and went overdue. Regression testing was not completed in time. The sprint 25 focus did not translate into delivery. |\n\n---\n\n### 2. EXP-002 — Customer Dashboard Redesign\n\n| Field | Value |\n|-------|-------|\n| Status | In Progress |\n| Priority | P2 — Medium |\n| Owner | Eve Thompson |\n| Period | 2025-09-15 → 2026-04-30 |\n| ⚠️ Past End Date | **YES** — ended 114 days ago (2026-04-30) |\n| Completion | 72.0% (18 / 25 tasks) |\n| Time Elapsed | 100.0% |\n| Completion Lag | **−28.0 points** |\n| Budget | $80,000 |\n| Budget Burn Rate | 72.0% |\n| Burn vs. Time | Critical: 72.0% spent, 100% elapsed — budget nearly depleted with 28% work remaining and deadline passed |\n| Health Signal | Behind |\n| ⚠️ Data Gap | No associated entries in run_log.csv — no run-level visibility |\n\n#### Open Incidents (Linked via Personnel)\n\n| Incident | Title | Severity | Status | Assignee/Reporter | Relevance |\n|----------|-------|----------|--------|-------------------|-----------|\n| INC-003 | Tooltip overlaps on mobile viewport | S3 — Minor | Open | Reporter: Eve Thompson | Low-severity UI cosmetic issue; unlikely to block completion but adds noise |\n| INC-005 | Dark mode toggle flickers | S4 — Trivial | Won't Fix | Reporter: Eve Thompson | Already closed per DEC-004 — listed for completeness |\n\n#### Overdue Runs\n\nNo runs found in run_log.csv associated with EXP-002. This confirms the data gap noted above — there is zero run-level task tracking visibility for this experiment.\n\n#### Discussion Threads & Unresolved Blockers\n\nNo discussion threads reference EXP-002 directly. The lack of threaded conversation correlates with the absence of task-level tracking.\n\n#### OKR Cross-Reference\n\nNo OKRs explicitly link to EXP-002. This is a strategic blind spot — a design-focused experiment operating without OKR alignment.\n\n#### Prior Decisions & Follow-Through\n\nNo prior decisions reference EXP-002.\n\n---\n\n### 3. EXP-004 — Security Audit 2026\n\n| Field | Value |\n|-------|-------|\n| Status | On Hold |\n| Priority | P0 — Critical |\n| Owner | Dave Wilson |\n| Period | 2026-02-01 → 2026-07-31 |\n| ⚠️ Past End Date | No (ends 2026-07-31 — 8 days from today) |\n| Completion | 20.0% (3 / 15 tasks) |\n| Time Elapsed | 65.0% |\n| Completion Lag | **−45.0 points** (worst deficit) |\n| Budget | $200,000 |\n| Budget Burn Rate | 20.0% |\n| Burn vs. Time | Under-burning relative to time: 20.0% spent, 65.0% elapsed — likely reflects On Hold status conserving spend |\n| Health Signal | Behind |\n\n#### Open Incidents (Linked via Personnel)\n\nNo open incidents in incident_log.csv assign Dave Wilson as assignee. Notable: INC-004 involved Dave Wilson as reporter (slow query issue), but resolved on 2026-04-08.\n\n#### Overdue Runs\n\n| Run | Title | Due Date | Days Overdue | Status | Priority |\n|-----|-------|----------|-------------|--------|----------|\n| RUN-008 | Audit third-party dependencies | 2026-05-30 | 84 days | To Do | High |\n\nOne high-priority run sitting in \"To Do\" for nearly three months despite P0 experiment priority.\n\n#### Discussion Threads & Unresolved Blockers\n\n| Thread | Key Issue | Status |\n|--------|-----------|--------|\n| Thread 6 (Security Documentation Gaps) | Three open gaps in access control documentation before May SOC 2 audit | **Critical:** SOC 2 audit was scheduled for May and has now passed unaddressed. The documentation gaps are unresolved. |\n\n#### OKR Cross-Reference\n\n| OKR | Objective | Status | Impact |\n|-----|-----------|--------|--------|\n| OKR-003 | Strengthen security & compliance | **Off Track** | SOC 2 Type II audit (KR1) likely missed. Zero critical incidents (KR2) depends on audit findings. SSO rollout (KR3) is stalled. This OKR is directly imperiled. |\n\n#### Prior Decisions & Follow-Through\n\n| Decision | Action Assigned | Acted On? | Assessment |\n|----------|----------------|-----------|------------|\n| **DEC-003** (2026-03-05) | Engage external compliance consultants to close documentation gaps before audit | ❌ **Action taken but outcome failed** | External help was requested, but the May SOC 2 audit deadline has passed and the experiment remains at 20%. Either the consultants did not arrive in time, their output was insufficient, or re-planning was never executed. |\n\n---\n\n### 4. EXP-005 — Mobile App Launch\n\n| Field | Value |\n|-------|-------|\n| Status | In Progress |\n| Priority | P1 — High |\n| Owners | Bob Martinez; Eve Thompson |\n| Period | 2025-06-01 → 2026-08-31 |\n| ⚠️ Past End Date | No (ends 2026-08-31) |\n| Completion | 66.7% (30 / 45 tasks) |\n| Time Elapsed | 79.4% |\n| Completion Lag | **−12.7 points** |\n| Budget | $250,000 |\n| Budget Burn Rate | 66.7% |\n| Burn vs. Time | Over-burning: 66.7% spent, 79.4% elapsed — 20.6% time window must deliver 33.3% of work |\n| Health Signal | At Risk |\n\n#### Open Incidents (Linked via Personnel)\n\n| Incident | Title | Severity | Status | Assignee/Reporter | Relevance |\n|----------|-------|----------|--------|-------------------|-----------|\n| INC-001 | Login page crashes on Safari 17 | S1 — Blocker | Fix In Progress | Bob Martinez | Shared assignee with EXP-001 — diverts attention from mobile work |\n| INC-003 | Tooltip overlaps on mobile viewport | S3 — Minor | Open | Reporter: Eve Thompson | Both owners span EXP-005 and EXP-002 — context switching between experiments |\n\n#### Overdue Runs\n\n| Run | Title | Due Date | Days Overdue | Status | Priority |\n|-----|-------|----------|-------------|--------|----------|\n| RUN-004 | Write E2E tests for checkout flow | 2026-05-17 | 67 days | In Progress | Urgent |\n| RUN-006 | Create onboarding tutorial screens | 2026-05-25 | 59 days | To Do | Medium |\n| RUN-007 | Implement push notification service | 2026-06-15 | 38 days | Backlog | Low |\n\nThree overdue tasks spanning urgent-to-low priorities. The E2E test gap (RUN-004) is the highest operational risk given its Urgent priority and late-stage testing implication.\n\n#### Discussion Threads & Unresolved Blockers\n\n| Thread | Key Issue | Status |\n|--------|-----------|--------|\n| Thread 3 (Mobile CI Flakiness) | iOS builds passing; Android payment module had flaky tests | Partially resolved — iOS stable, Android race condition scoped |\n| Thread 5 (Mobile Beta Scope) | Tight timeline for 1,000-user beta; scope down onboarding | **Decision rendered** (DEC-002) |\n\n#### OKR Cross-Reference\n\n| OKR | Objective | Status | Impact |\n|-----|-----------|--------|--------|\n| OKR-002 | Deliver best-in-class mobile experience | **At Risk** | All three KRs affected: beta user target, crash rate (<2% on launch day), and app store rating depend on completing the remaining 33% of tasks within 20.6% time. CI instability and overdue E2E tests pose direct threat to KR2 and KR3. |\n\n#### Prior Decisions & Follow-Through\n\n| Decision | Action Assigned | Acted On? | Assessment |\n|----------|----------------|-----------|------------|\n| **DEC-002** (2026-04-16) | Ship minimal onboarding; iterate post-launch | ✅ Appears acted upon | Scope reduction aligns with moving the beta forward. However, the overall project remains 12.7 points behind, suggesting scoping alone was insufficient to recover schedule. |\n\n---\n\n## Summary Table — All Flagged Items\n\n| Experiment | Title | Completion Lag | Days Past Deadline* | Active Incidents | Overdue Runs | Budget | Burn Rate | Linked OKR | OKR Status |\n|------------|-------|---------------|---------------------|------------------|--------------|--------|-----------|------------|------------|\n| EXP-001 | API v2 Migration | −26.7 | 54 | 2 (1 S1 Blocker) | 2 | $150K | 60.0% | OKR-001 | On Track ⚠️ |\n| EXP-002 | Customer Dashboard Redesign | −28.0 | 114 | 1 (S3 Minor) | 0† | $80K | 72.0% | None | N/A † |\n| EXP-004 | Security Audit 2026 | −45.0 | 0‡ | 0 | 1 (P0 run) | $200K | 20.0% | OKR-003 | Off Track 🔴 |\n| EXP-005 | Mobile App Launch | −12.7 | 0§ | 2 (1 S1 shared) | 3 | $250K | 66.7% | OKR-002 | At Risk 🟡 |\n\n\\* Past deadline calculated from experiment end_date to today (2026-07-23).  \n‡ EXP-004 ends 2026-07-31 — 8 days away.  \n§ EXP-005 ends 2026-08-31 — 39 days away.  \n† EXP-002 has no run-level tracking data and no OKR linkage.\n\n### Cost Exposure Snapshot\n\n| Metric | Value |\n|--------|-------|\n| Total committed budget (flagged experiments) | $680,000 |\n| Deployed so far | $430,000 |\n| Remaining to deploy | $250,000 |\n| Work remaining (estimate based on completion) | ~21 of 55 total tasks (~38%) |\n| Avg. burn-rate excess over time elapsed | EXP-001: +13.3pts; EXP-002: +28.0pts; EXP-005: +12.7pts |\n\n---\n\n## Recommendations\n\n### Immediate (Next 7 Days)\n\n1. **EXP-002 executive escalation.** 114 days past deadline, no task tracking, no OKR alignment. Determine whether to restart planning, extend the mandate, or sunset and reassign resources.\n\n2. **EXP-004 crisis session with Dave Wilson.** The May SOC 2 audit is unmissable. DEC-003's external consultant engagement produced no visible results. Decide: bring in new expertise, extend the audit, or accept non-compliance for H1.\n\n3. **Free Bob Martinez from INC-001 triage conflict.** He owns both EXP-001's core migration AND is the fix-owner on an S1 blocker. Split the load or escalate ownership. Context switching between these priorities is accelerating the lag on both fronts.\n\n### Short-Term (Next 30 Days)\n\n4. **Kick off overdue-run cleanup sprints for EXP-001 and EXP-005.** Combine RUN-001/RUN-002 into a focused 2-week closure push. For EXP-005, prioritize RUN-004 (E2E tests, Urgent) before any new feature development.\n\n5. **Restore run-level tracking for EXP-002.** Every experiment with budget allocation should have task-level visibility. Add backlog items immediately even if retroactive.\n\n6. **OKR-003 recovery plan.** With the experiment at 20% and the audit passed, reassess whether SOC 2 Type II can be pursued in H2 or if interim controls suffice for enterprise customer commitments.\n\n7. **Budget reallocation review.** EXP-004 is burning slowly (20%) due to On Hold status — consider redirecting uncommitted funds to EXP-005's remaining tasks, which need coverage in the final 20% time window.\n\n### Structural\n\n8. **Institute monthly lag reviews.** A −10-point delta is the current threshold for flagging, but two experiments exceeded −25. Consider tighter cadence (biweekly) once delta crosses −20.\n\n9. **Bind incidents to experiments explicitly.** The current personnel-overlap linkage methodology introduces ambiguity. Add `experiment_id` to `incident_log.csv` to eliminate guessing.\n\n10. **Require OKR linkage for every budgeted experiment.** EXP-002 operates at $80K with no strategic tether — this pattern risks orphan projects consuming budget with no measurable outcome.\n"}
