[rank0]:Here are examples of how to call functions in the tool set. To make parallel tool calls, emit each call as its own message (one tool call per message) in consecutive messages, as shown below:
[rank0]:(If the tool namespace is not specified, invoke the function directly as `example_function_name_1` rather than `example_tool_name_1.example_function_name_1`)
[rank0]:
[rank0]:to=example_tool_name_1.example_function_name_1
[rank0]:
[rank0]:<atem:function_calls>
[rank0]:<atem:invoke name="example_tool_name_1.example_function_name_1">
[rank0]:<atem:parameter name="example_parameter_1">value_1</atem:parameter>
[rank0]:</atem:invoke>
[rank0]:</atem:function_calls>
[rank0]:
[rank0]:to=example_tool_name_2.example_function_name_2
[rank0]:
[rank0]:<atem:function_calls>
[rank0]:<atem:invoke name="example_tool_name_2.example_function_name_2">
[rank0]:<atem:parameter name="example_parameter_2">This is the value for the second parameter
[rank0]:that can span
[rank0]:"multiple" lines
[rank0]:</atem:parameter>
[rank0]:<atem:parameter name="example_parameter_3">value_3</atem:parameter>
[rank0]:</atem:invoke>
[rank0]:</atem:function_calls>
[rank0]:
[rank0]:Reasoning strength: 32.
[rank0]:
[rank0]:Use the appropriate recipient for each message:
[rank0]:
[rank0]:- "self": private reasoning and tool planning.
[rank0]:- "commentary": user-visible intermediate updates while the assistant will continue working, including messages sent to the user before or between tool calls.
[rank0]:- "tool" or "[tool name]": the name of the tool to call.
[rank0]:- "user": messages that end the assistant turn, such as a completed response or clarification question that waits for the user's reply; do not use for pre-tool updates or partial responses.
[rank0]:
[rank0]:# Valid recipients: "self", "commentary", "[func_name] (e.g., read)", "user".<|eot|><|start|>user<|message|>Our wellness app has a batch of 5 upcoming client consultation slots listed in consultation_schedule.json. For each scheduled appointment, I need you to perform a traditional divination reading based on that specific appointment time and compile all results into a single file called divination_report.json. Each entry in the report should clearly associate the client and their appointment slot with the full reading outcome, including the three palace results and the interpretive meaning for the hour palace.<|eot|><|start|>assistant to=self<|message|>The user wants me to:
[rank0]:1. Read a file called `consultation_schedule.json` that has 5 upcoming client consultation slots
[rank0]:2. For each appointment, perform a "traditional divination reading" based on the appointment time
[rank0]:3. Compile results into `divination_report.json`
[rank0]:
[rank0]:Let me first find and read the consultation schedule file, then understand what "traditional divination" means in this context (likely Chinese astrology/Chinese zodiac based on "palace" terminology).
[rank0]:
[rank0]:Let me start by reading the consultation schedule.<|eom|><|start|>assistant to=exec<|message|><atem:function_calls>
[rank0]:<atem:invoke name="exec">
[rank0]:<atem:parameter name="command">find /home/node/.openclaw/workspace -name "consultation_schedule.json" 2&gt;/dev/null; find / -name "consultation_schedule.json" 2&gt;/dev/null | head -5</atem:parameter>
[rank0]:</atem:invoke>
[rank0]:</atem:function_calls><|eot|><|start|>tool exec<|message|><tool_output name="exec">
[rank0]:{"result": "Command still running (session tidal-gulf, pid 278). Use process (list/poll/log/write/kill/clear/remove) for follow-up."}
[rank0]:</tool_output><|eot|><|start|>assistant to=self<|message|>The command is still running. Let me wait for it to complete.<|eom|><|start|>assistant to=process<|message|><atem:function_calls>
[rank0]:<atem:invoke name="process">
[rank0]:<atem:parameter name="action">poll</atem:parameter>
[rank0]:<atem:parameter name="sessionId">tidal-gulf</atem:parameter>
[rank0]:<atem:parameter name="timeout">5000</atem:parameter>
[rank0]:</atem:invoke>
[rank0]:</atem:function_calls><|eot|><|start|>tool process<|message|><tool_output name="process">
[rank0]:{"result": "/home/node/.openclaw/workspace/consultation_schedule.json\n\nProcess still running."}
[rank0]:</tool_output><|eot|><|start|>assistant to=self<|message|>Found the file. Let me read it.<|eom|><|start|>assistant to=process<|message|><atem:function_calls>
[rank0]:<atem:invoke name="process">
